- `branch(b1, XOR)`, `action(n5, "No hardware issues found")`, `action(n7, "Conclude hardware inspection without repair")`, `converge(c1)`: Hallucinates a conditional split and merge not present in the source. The description specifies a linear progression ("proceed with repairing any issues that were identified... conclude the hardware inspection... test the functionality"), with no alternative path for when no issues exist (SMC1, SMC4).
- `branch(b2, XOR)`, `precedence(b2, n10)`, `precedence(b2, n11)`: Omits required `guard(...)` statements to encode the explicit decision criteria described in the source ("If the test results indicate that everything is functioning properly...", "if the test results indicate that there are still issues...") (SMC1, SMC4).
- `defines(v1, "Identify hardware issues", {})`, `defines(v2, "Are system tests successful", {})`: Both decision variables are assigned empty value ranges `{}`, failing to reflect the binary/pass-fail nature of the source conditions and leaving them semantically undefined for use in guards (SMC6).
